{"date":"2026-11-02T19:43:22Z","latency_ms":5985,"model":"gemini-3.1-flash-lite","query":"clean up and organize these notes","response":{"status":"requires_action","usage":{"total_tokens":16979,"total_input_tokens":14858,"input_tokens_by_modality":[{"modality":"text","tokens":14858}],"total_cached_tokens":12194,"cached_tokens_by_modality":[{"modality":"text","tokens":12194}],"total_output_tokens":300,"total_tool_use_tokens":0,"total_thought_tokens":1821,"initial_input_tokens":13526},"created":"2026-11-02T19:43:22Z","updated":"2026-11-02T19:43:22Z","service_tier":"standard","steps":[{"signature":"","type":"thought"},{"id":"call_133476","type":"function_call","name":"notebook","arguments":{"query":"clean up and organize these notes","action":"replace","text":"## Project Ideas\n\n- Calendar should come first, because it is the one thing I open every single day and it needs to work with the calendars I already use.\n- He should be curious about my life, for example asking how the dentist went a week after I mention it.\n- I want him on the laptop as well as the phone, so that it feels like one assistant wherever I happen to be sitting.\n- He should not just wait for commands; if he notices the oven timer is about to go off he can say so without being asked.\n- When I ask for something silly he should play along for a moment and then actually do it properly, and know what he is good at.\n- When I change a list he should notice what is new and offer to help with it later on.\n- When the room is quiet he should lower his voice without me having to ask for it.\n- Remember to look at how real secretaries keep their notes, and talk to one if I can find someone willing.\n- Maybe ask a comedy writer to read his lines, since the humour is the whole point of having a character at all.\n- The timer has to be reliable, and I should be able to set one with my hands full while I am cooking dinner.","note":"n1"}}],"object":"interaction","model":"gemini-3.1-flash-lite"}}